{
    "version": "2026-10-08",
    "notes": [
        "What each carrier can do with duties terms to each destination (ADR-0008 decision 4).",
        "support is ddp_required (ships there only with duties prepaid), either, or ddu_only",
        "(cannot prepay duties there). A rate whose support does not fit the Shipment's",
        "resolved duties term is dropped with the reason named, never forced to the other term.",
        "",
        "Carrier keys are matched through CarrierAlias::lookupKey against the canonical carrier",
        "name. A carrier not listed here is not filtered. Each carrier has a default for the",
        "countries it does not list, and an authority: the short name a dropped rate's reason",
        "cites. Every entry, default included, names its source (an https URL, or a path in this",
        "repository) and the date it was checked.",
        "",
        "An entry with effective_from later than the day of the quote is ignored until that day,",
        "and the carrier's default applies meanwhile. Bump version whenever an entry changes.",
        "",
        "USPS is the International Mail Manual's DDP table (IMM 360) for Priority Mail Express",
        "International, Priority Mail International and First-Class Package International. LU is",
        "in none of its lists, so it takes the default. UPS and FedEx express accepted DDU",
        "throughout the EU as of 2026-10-01; international-customs-terms/02 verifies both terms",
        "against their APIs."
    ],
    "carriers": {
